    <txtName>NORDHOLZ 2</txtName>
    <txtNameAlt>ETMN A4460 123.300</txtNameAlt>
    <codeDistVerUpper>ALT</codeDistVerUpper>
    <valDistVerUpper>5000</valDistVerUpper>
    <uomDistVerUpper>FT</uomDistVerUpper>
    <codeDistVerLower>ALT</codeDistVerLower>
    <valDistVerLower>1500</valDistVerLower>
    <uomDistVerLower>FT</uomDistVerLower>
    <codeSelAvbl>Y</codeSelAvbl>
    <txtRmk>The times of activity depend to those of the Nordholz control zone.
The following information on the times of activity gives a rough indication concerning the expected activation: 
Mon – Thu: 0700 (0600) – 2200 (2100), Fri 0700 (0600) – 1200 (1100).
Activation outside the times published and/or deactivation within these times is possible at all times
and will be announced by NOTAM.
Information about the current status of RMZ Nordholz can be requested on frequencies 
122.100 MHz (NORDHOLZ TURM), 123.300 MHz (NORDHOLZ RADAR) or 128.525 / 125.100 MHz (LANGEN INFORMATION).
Exemptions from this obligation can be approved by telephone or by radiotelephony by the competent air
traffic services unit on NORDHOLZ RADAR 123.300 MHz if the safety of air traffic is not impaired.

Sailplanes and other manned aircraft and air sports equipment which are not equipped with a transponder are
exempt from the mandatory carriage of a transponder and shall follow the provisions laid down for the RMZ (radio mandatory zone) Nordholz.</txtRmk>
