  <Ase>
    <AseUid mid="5abeaf7e-7431-e0d5-3aea-6d6b4429021c" region="ED">
      <codeType>RMZ</codeType>
      <codeId>ED2F91B</codeId>
    </AseUid>
    <txtName>NORDHOLZ 2</txtName>
    <txtNameAlt>ETMN 123.300</txtNameAlt>
    <codeClass>E</codeClass>
    <codeDistVerUpper>ALT</codeDistVerUpper>
    <valDistVerUpper>5000</valDistVerUpper>
    <uomDistVerUpper>FT</uomDistVerUpper>
    <codeDistVerLower>ALT</codeDistVerLower>
    <valDistVerLower>1500</valDistVerLower>
    <uomDistVerLower>FT</uomDistVerLower>
    <codeSelAvbl>Y</codeSelAvbl>
    <txtRmk>The following regulations apply only to sailplanes and other manned
aircraft and air sports equipment which are not equipped with a transponder.

The times of activity depend to those of the Nordholz control zone.
The following information on the times of activity gives a rough indication concerning the expected activation:
Mon – Thu: 0700 (0600) – 2200 (2100), Fri 0700 (0600) – 1200 (1100).
Activation outside the times published and/or deactivation within these times is possible at all times and will be announced by NOTAM.
Information about the current status of RMZ Nordholz can be requested on frequencies 
122.100 MHz (NORDHOLZ TURM), 123.300 MHz (NORDHOLZ RADAR) or 128.525 / 125.100 MHz (LANGEN INFORMATION).</txtRmk>
  </Ase>
